%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
CASE I:
naca_set_e2048.re2:= naca_o_sharp_e2048_c80_2d.re2
naca_set_e2048.re2:= naca_run_e2048.re2
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

  Step1
   - Set SIZE. Has to be lx1=4, lxd=5 !!!
   - ./makenek naca_set_e2048
   - ./nekmpi naca_set_e2048 1
   - will generate geom_3x3_e2048.dat


  Step2
   - Set SIZE lx1=6, lxd=9 or else.
   - ./makenek naca_run_e2048
   - ./nekmpi naca_run_e2048 #np

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
CASE II (original, Paul Fischer's toy reference case -- superseded below):
naca_set_e448.re2:= naca_o_sharp_e448_c4_2d.re2
naca_set_e448.re2:= naca_run_e448.re2
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

  Step1
   - Set SIZE. Has to be lx1=4, lxd=5 !!!
   - ./makenek naca_set_e448
   - ./nekmpi naca_set_e448 1
   - will generate geom_3x3_e448.dat


  Step2
   - Set SIZE lx1=6, lxd=9 or else.
   - ./makenek naca_run_e448
   - ./nekmpi naca_run_e448 #np

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
AeroHexMesh adaptation (this repo, replaces CASE II above):
naca_gen_spline_info.{usr,par} -- Fischer's smooth_geom0 wall-smoothing
algorithm, adapted for meshes generated by this repo's own
p3d_to_gmsh_nek.py + gmsh2nek + genmap (see ../../README.md), not his
original e448 toy mesh. The case name was renamed from naca_set_e448 to be
purpose-descriptive rather than tied to a specific (and now irrelevant)
element count.

smooth_geom0 originally only handled an O-grid's closed wall loop. It's
been generalized to also handle a C-grid's open (or, for a sharp trailing
edge, wake-cut-fold-closed) wall sub-range -- see the WALL_START_ELEMENT /
WALL_ELEMENT_COUNT #defines below and the comments directly above
smooth_geom0 in the .usr file for how that works. This directory is
currently configured for a C-grid case (naca0012_sharp.p3d/.nmf); an
O-grid mesh works too, it just needs different #define values (see below).
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

  Step1 -- generates the wall-spline correction data later applied to the
  real 3D mesh in ../../high_order_mesh/example_nekrs/ (get_smooth_data).

   - Set SIZE. Has to be lx1=4, lxd=5 !!!

   - Set #define NUMBER_ELEMENTS_X/_Y, WALL_START_ELEMENT and
     WALL_ELEMENT_COUNT at the top of naca_gen_spline_info.usr to match
     the actual mesh. Don't compute these by hand -- run, from
     linear_mesh/:
         python3 compute_case_params.py <airfoil>.nmf --smoothing-levels 1 \
             --patch-step1-usr smooth_2D/naca_gen_spline_info.usr
     (NUMBER_ELEMENTS_Y here means "how many near-wall rings to actually
     spline-correct", not the mesh's total radial ring count -- that's
     why --smoothing-levels needs to be given explicitly, typically 1.)

   - Build the 2D mesh this case reads (naca_gen_spline_info.re2) via
     p3d_to_gmsh_nek.py + Gmsh order elevation + gmsh2nek -- see
     ../../README.md's "Running it end to end" section -- and copy it in.

   - genmap (interactively: case name, tolerance) to produce the .ma2

   - ./makenek naca_gen_spline_info
   - ./nekmpi naca_gen_spline_info 1
   - will generate geom_3x3_naca_gen_spline_info.dat
   - "EXIT: smooth_geom SUCCESS!" followed by a non-zero shell exit is
     expected -- that's how this case signals successful completion

  Step2 -- applies the correction generated above to the real 3D mesh and
  runs the actual flow solve. See
  ../../high_order_mesh/example_nekrs/README (or ../../README.md) --
  it's a separate NekRS case, not run from this directory.
